{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And it was told Laban on the third day.</b> There was a distance of three days' journey between the flocks of Jacob and the flocks of Laban, and when the informer went to tell Laban on the third day, Laban took his kinsmen with him and returned from the place of the flocks to Paddan — behold, six days: three days of the informer and three of Laban's return journey, and on the seventh day he caught up with him. That is what is written: ״וירדף אחריו דרך שבעת ימים״ — 'and he pursued him a seven days' journey.' It follows that all that Jacob traveled in six days, Laban traveled in one day, as Rashi wrote. And it is possible that Jacob began his journey from Paddan-aram on the first day, and the seventh day on which Laban traveled and caught up with him was the Sabbath."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:38.923520517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}